WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.160
Russia has massed military&nbsp;
forces on Ukraine’s borders.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:13.120
But Putin denies he’ll invade. His demands are&nbsp;
about much more than Ukraine. What’s going on?

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:18.560
Putin is holding Ukraine hostage. He&nbsp;
demands NATO never expand to the east.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:22.560
That NATO pull its military forces from&nbsp;
members that joined after the Cold War.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:25.600
And that NATO never deploy certain&nbsp;
weapons near Russia’s borders.

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:28.080
In return, he promises…nothing.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.520
Putin wants to regain control of Ukraine of&nbsp;
course. But, more than that, he wants to destroy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:42.240
NATO. He wants to divide east European members&nbsp;
from their west European allies. To split the US&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:49.720
from Europe. To regain Russian hegemony. Those&nbsp;
are his real goals in this manufactured crisis.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:58.240
The US must stand by its alliance commitments. It&nbsp;
must stand with Ukraine. It must stand with NATO.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:02.800
If we give in to Putin’s demands, it will be open&nbsp;
season for aggressive dictators around the world.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:05.040
It will be disastrous for America.

00:01:07.177 --> 00:01:11.264
Do you think the US should stand up to Putin? Let us know in our poll.

00:01:11.264 --> 00:01:16.056
Also, let us know what other topics you'd like our scholars to cover in 60 seconds,

00:01:16.056 --> 00:01:20.580
and be sure to like and subscribe for more research and videos from AEI.

